--- body ---
## Context

DECISIONS.md's 2026-09-01 entry (see also ticket 0028's log, same date) rules
a second segmentation path for the acceptance test's wider corpus (books,
proceedings, dictionaries, handbooks, encyclopedias, 40+ page PDFs, explicitly
multilingual -- EN/FR/VN MUST). Above a length threshold, zoteus reaches for
the PDF attachment itself instead of Zotero's flat fulltext cache, and hands
it to a vendored `pdf.js`-based segmenter (Apache-2.0; `PyMuPDF`/`fitz`
explicitly rejected -- AGPL-3.0-or-commercial against zoteus's MIT license).

Evidence: `verification/SEGMENTER-FIELD-REVIEW-0028.md` (three research
passes) and the DECISIONS.md ruling and its same-day correction.

**Sequencing, ruled by the author in the same session**: seg/1 (ticket 0028)
ships first -- a simple segmenter working on the flat text file -- because it
solves integration (chunk-key identity, the confidence/synthetic-fallback
pattern, wiring into X5 and the entries table) that every child here would
otherwise have to solve a second time, or worse, solve once badly and redo.
Everything in this tracker is improvement on a working baseline, not a
parallel track.

## Children, in the order they become buildable once 0028 ships

1. `0558` -- attachment file access (stored + linked PDFs via the local API)
2. `0559` -- length trigger (indexedPages -> page-break count -> char-count
   estimate)
3. `0560` -- vendor `pdf.js`, tier 1: embedded TOC extraction
4. `0561` -- tier 2: layout heading heuristic on `pdf.js` text runs; falls
   through to seg/1 on low confidence, no third PDF-side fallback
5. `0562` -- byline/author detection layer (deferred, DECISIONS.md 2026-09-02)
6. `0563` -- language robustness (NFC normalization, legacy-encoding sanity
   check, EN/FR/VN fixtures)
7. `0564` -- segmenter identity + the PDF-path-vs-seg/1 selection rule

`0558` through `0560` have no dependency on each other and can run in
parallel once unblocked. `0561` benefits from `0560` existing (shares the
`pdf.js` text-run primitives) but does not strictly require it to be
finished. `0564` is the integration point and is naturally last -- it needs
both a working seg/1 (0028) and at least tier 1 (0560) to have something to
select between.

## Invariants

- No new copyleft (GPL/AGPL) dependency vendored into zoteus (MIT).
- seg/1 is never removed or degraded by this work; it remains the fallback
  for sub-threshold documents and PDF-access failures.
- No third, PDF-side fixed-size fallback tier (ruled out 2026-09-01) --
  low-confidence tier 2 falls through to seg/1, not to a duplicate mechanism.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] 0028 closed
- [ ] every child closed or explicitly disposed of — 0562 is deferred by the
      2026-09-02 byline ruling and 0561 is absorbed by 0606, so "all seven
      closed" was unsatisfiable as written; each non-closed child needs a
      recorded disposition, not a tick
- [ ] integration review: re-read child diffs, run the full suite, verify
      the selection rule actually prefers the PDF path above the threshold
      and falls back to seg/1 correctly, before this tracker closes
